      "description": "Importing Item Response Theory (IRT) from educational measurement into LLM evaluation, then extending the psychometric model to capture LLM-specific phenomena (multidimensional ability, item redundancy, difficulty-guided generation). The pattern works because LLMs exhibit the same latent-trait structure as human test-takers (metabench's single factor captures 79.3% of variance), making IRT assumptions empirically valid. Success comes from going beyond naive application — the winning papers adapt IRT to the LLM setting with novel estimation procedures or novel uses of IRT parameters.",
