  "reviewer_preferences": [
    "Theoretical grounding with formal models: Papers accepted at top venues consistently anchor their contributions in formal frameworks (IRT models in metabench/tinyBenchmarks, conformal inference in JECS, weight decay bounds in 'How Much Can We Forget'). Ad-hoc empirical studies without theoretical backing get lower-tier acceptances. RIDE's IRT-as-reward-signal and GenPRM's RPE formalization both received strong reviews specifically because reviewers valued the mathematical grounding.",
